\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Before Jehovah's awful throne,
\par Ye nations, bow with sacred joy:
\par Know that the Lord is God alone;
\par He can create, and He destroy.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. His sovereign power, without our aid,
\par Made us of clay, and formed us men;
\par And when like wandering sheep we strayed,
\par He brought us to His fold again.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. We'll crowd Thy gates with thankful songs;
\par High as the Heavens our voices raise;
\par And earth, with her ten thousand tongues,
\par Shall fill Thy courts with sounding praise.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Wide as the world is Thy command;
\par Vast as eternity Thy love;
\par Firm as a rock Thy truth shall stand,
\par When rolling years shall cease to move.
\par                                                  Amen!.
\par \cf1\ul\b\f1\fs16 
\par 
\par }

